  "assumptions": [
    "Reprice recorded usage at the dated standard global retail rates, not historical invoices. No report-time network access is required.",
    "Anthropic cache writes use the five-minute rate. OpenAI models with explicit write pricing use the 30-minute rate; models without separate write pricing use ordinary input pricing. Models without cache discounts use ordinary input pricing.",
    "Recorded cache counts, including explicit zero, take precedence. Missing cache counts are unknown, not observed zero.",
    "When missing, cache reads may be estimated as the previous request's input, capped by available input, only for the same source, harness, session and model, a nonshrinking context, and a positive gap of at most five minutes. This assumes append-only context reuse; token counts do not prove an identical prefix or a cache hit.",
    "Inferred-cache point estimates assume no unrecorded cache writes. Missing-cache cost ranges allocate unknown input between fresh tokens, cache reads and cache writes at the minimum/maximum applicable rates. Ranges are sensitivity bounds, not confidence intervals.",
    "Without eligible consecutive context evidence, show only a range; do not assume an arbitrary cached-input percentage. Missing total input/output or an unknown model rate remains unpriced.",
    "Exclude subscriptions, credits, tool fees, compute, storage, taxes, discounts, regional premiums, and fast-mode premiums. These are API-equivalent estimates, not actual billed spend.",
    "GPT-5.6 Sol promotional retail rates are scheduled through 2026-11-30; this is a frozen 2026-11-13 snapshot, not live pricing."
